11a. Programming example for MySQLin Docker
MySQL — SQL Commands in CLI
Step 1: Start MySQL on Killercoda

docker run --name mysql-test -e MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD=root -d -p 3306:3306 mysql

Step 2: Enter MySQL CLI

docker exec -it mysql-test mysql -uroot -proot

Step 3: Run SQL Commands (directly in terminal)

CREATE DATABASE testdb;
USE testdb;
CREATE TABLE users (
id VARCHAR(10) PRIMARY KEY,
name VARCHAR(50),
age INT
);

//Now Insert The values :

INSERT INTO users VALUES ('u001', 'Alice', 30);
INSERT INTO users VALUES ('u002', 'Bob', 25);

Now Display the table contents:
SELECT * FROM users;
